## Rules (from the Vibe Coding Governance Toolkit)
- Follow the `safe-vibe-coding` skill.
- Ask before deleting, moving, overwriting, or resetting anything, and list exactly what will be affected.
- Work only on the development copy with test data. Never connect to production.
- Never ask me to paste passwords, keys, or tokens into the chat. Never write them into code.
- Make one small change at a time and tell me how to check it worked.
- Never make up data or results. If you didn't run something, say so.
- Add a limit and an off switch to any loop, schedule, agent, or email sending.
- Don't run tests, scanners, or deployments without my explicit OK.
